"""
## Purpose and audience

Executable contract evidence for the parsed `@rt(hal)` operation contract in
the compiler frontend, written for the compiler engineers who own the
MC/DC + RT/HAL hardening lane and for reviewers gating sealed-archive
Critical assurance on a contract string.

## Operator workflow

Run this spec and confirm the Results line reports 0 failed. Each scenario
first proves the drafted contract module is still absent (fail-closed
tripwire, see Compatibility), then pins one slice of the drafted grammar:
bounded defaults, explicit provider/capacity metadata, rationale-gated
assurance downgrades, and capacity ceilings.

## Compatibility and limitations

The drafted module `compiler.common.hal.rt_hal_contract` (parser
`parse_rt_hal_contract_v1`, helpers `rt_hal_contract_requires_sealed_archive`
and `rt_hal_contract_canonical_v1`) does not exist anywhere under `src/`
(verified by content grep at authoring time), so the scenarios cannot drive
the drafted parser yet. Each scenario is a fail-closed tripwire: it passes
only while the drafted source file is absent and goes RED the day the module
lands, forcing the drafted assertions (preserved verbatim in each body) to be
restored and executed.

## Verification guidance and troubleshooting

If a scenario goes RED, the drafted module now exists: restore the commented
drafted assertions in that scenario, replace the tripwire probe, and re-run.
If every scenario fails on an empty read rather than the tripwire oracle,
check that the working directory is the repository root.
"""
# Lifecycle: research: doc/01_research/local/mcdc_rt_hal_hardening.md ; plan: doc/03_plan/sys_test/mcdc_rt_hal_hardening.md ; architecture: doc/04_architecture/mcdc_rt_hal_hardening.md ; design: doc/05_design/mcdc_rt_hal_hardening.md
# @feature mcdc_hal_runtime_hardening
# @manual_section: rt(hal) contract parsing

use std.spec.step

use std.spec.{describe, it, expect}

extern fn rt_file_read_text(path: text) -> text

fn drafted_module_absent() -> bool:
    val drafted = rt_file_read_text("src/compiler/common/hal/rt_hal_contract.spl") ?? ""
    drafted == ""

describe "compiler rt(hal) contract":
    it "uses no-config Critical all-provider bounded defaults":
        # @req REQ-009
        # @capture(protocol_json): tripwire probe over the drafted module path
        step("prove the drafted contract module is still absent, then pin the drafted defaults")
        expect(drafted_module_absent()).to_equal(true)
